1
00:00:00,175 --> 00:00:03,849
Everyone swore light was tiny bullets—until two beams crossed and created darkness.

2
00:00:04,625 --> 00:00:06,732
Light travels straight! Mere particles!

3
00:00:07,075 --> 00:00:09,237
Then watch it bend like ripples, Sir Isaac.

4
00:00:09,625 --> 00:00:15,034
In 1678, Christiaan Huygens proved every point on a wavefront sparks fresh baby ripples—forming interference.

5
00:00:15,625 --> 00:00:18,149
Inside Iceland spar crystal, one beam splits in two!

6
00:00:18,475 --> 00:00:20,214
Impossible! Bullets don't ripple!

7
00:00:20,625 --> 00:00:24,996
He also built the pendulum clock and unveiled Saturn's rings with wave-honed lenses.

8
00:00:25,625 --> 00:00:29,385
Lasers, Wi-Fi, and 5G today? All surfing Huygens' waves.
